HSA Receipt Processor (Rust Worker)
A high-performance, asynchronous background worker built in Rust to handle medical receipt OCR processing. This worker acts as the "Core" processing engine for the ActualBridge HSA management ecosystem.

🏗 Architecture
This project follows a Hybrid Cloud pattern, leveraging the strengths of two distinct ecosystems:

Edge (C# / .NET): Handles user authentication, API management, and the web frontend.

Core (Rust): A stateless, high-concurrency worker that manages the resource-intensive OCR pipeline and data integrity.

🧠 The 3-Tiered Intelligent Cascading Pipeline
Rather than relying solely on expensive cloud APIs, the worker implements a resilient, cost-optimized Semantic Routing / Cascading Fallback pattern to evaluate and repair receipt data:

[ Azure Queue Request ]
         │
         ▼
 ┌───────────────┐
 │    TIER 1     │ ──(Confidence ≥ 70%)──► [ Success: Persist Metadata ]
 │ Local Text    │
 └───────────────┘
         │ (Low Confidence)
         ▼
 ┌───────────────┐
 │    TIER 2     │ ──(Confidence ≥ 70%)──► [ Success: Persist Metadata ]
 │ OpenAI Repair │
 └───────────────┘
         │ (Validation Fails / Low Confidence)
         ▼
 ┌───────────────┐
 │    TIER 3     │ ──────────────────────► [ Success: Persist Metadata ]
 │  Azure Cloud  │
 └───────────────┘

 Tier 1: Local Image Pre-Processing & Tesseract (Free/Edge)
The worker applies grayscale conversion, resolution downscaling (to a max 2000px boundary), and aggressive contrast adjustments (Luma8 binarization) to incoming receipt images. This strips away shadows, table backgrounds, and color noise, allowing local Tesseract OCR to extract maximum fidelity at zero compute cost.

Tier 2: OpenAI Semantic Audit & Data Repair (Low Cost)
If local OCR yields a confidence score below 0.70, the raw text is forwarded to gpt-4o-mini. Driven by strict schema prompts, the AI fixes broken text formatting, validates fields, and infers financial Expense Categories (e.g., Meals, Software, Medical Utilities).

Tier 3: Azure Document Intelligence Fallback (Premium Cloud)
If the LLM flags the receipt as structurally invalid or confidence remains below the threshold, the system escalates the raw image to the premium Azure Document Intelligence (Prebuilt-Receipt Model) as the ultimate source of truth.

Fault-Tolerant Queue Bounds: If a total provider dropout occurs and all three tiers exhaustively fail, the error is safely swallowed and logged. The message is intentionally preserved on the Azure Queue, allowing it to become visible again for retry without data loss.

🚀 Key Features
Memory Efficient: Processes image bytes entirely in-memory to minimize I/O overhead.

Type-Safe OCR: Uses a custom OcrEngine trait, allowing for seamless swapping between Azure AI and local engines (like Tesseract).

Resilient Metadata: Aligns with C# MedicalReceipt schemas, ensuring the Blob Storage remains a searchable "Source of Truth."

Fully Mocked Suite: Unit tests utilize mockito to simulate complex Azure AI lifecycles without incurring cloud costs.

🛠 Tech Stack
Language: Rust (Latest Stable)

Async Runtime: tokio

Image Processing: image (v0.25)

Cloud SDKs: azure_storage_blobs, azure_storage_queues, async-openai

Serialization: serde, serde_json

🚦 Getting Started
📦 Development Container Setup
The easiest way to work on this repository is using VS Code and Docker via the Dev Containers extension. The included container environment comes pre-configured with the required native C libraries (tesseract, leptonica, pkg-config, and LLVM compilers) so you can hit the ground running without local installation friction.

Open the project folder in VS Code.

Click "Reopen in Container" when prompted (or open the Command Palette Ctrl+Shift+P and select Dev Containers: Reopen in Container).

The environment will assemble automatically, and your workspace will be fully ready for compilation.

Environment Variables
Copy .env.example to a new file named .env and fill in your target infrastructure keys:

# Azure Storage Infrastructure
AZURE_STORAGE_CONNECTION_STRING="DefaultEndpointsProtocol=https;AccountName=...;AccountKey=..."
AZURE_QUEUE_NAME="receipt-requests"
AZURE_CONTAINER_NAME="receipts"

# Azure Document Intelligence (OCR Fallback)
AZURE_DOC_INTEL_ENDPOINT="https://your-resource.cognitiveservices.azure.com/"
AZURE_DOC_INTEL_KEY="your-api-key"

# OpenAI Auditor Gateway
OPENAI_API_KEY="your-openai-api-key"

Running the Worker
cargo run --release

Running Tests
cargo test